{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Her [I have designated] as proof.</b> The servant relied on the prayer of the prophet, which HaShem answered him, and he was proven in a dream by means of the angel who is HaShem's emissary to help him. The servant thought in his heart that there is no family as generous as his master's family, and many are astonished, saying that he did not ask properly — but I do not know why, for if there had been another girl who would give him drink and water his camels, and it turned out that she was from a different family, he would have left her and lost nothing. For <b>\"Whose daughter are you\"</b> — its meaning is that he already said to her before he gave her anything; and likewise he said <b>\"I asked her,\"</b> <b>\"I placed the ring\"</b>. The upshot of the matter is that he prayed to HaShem that He would prove [her to be] one of his master's family, and the proof would come about in the way of character, as befitting a generous man's daughter. And HaShem heard his prayer. And Jonathan's way is different:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:37.969615760Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}